# Frontend Constraints

Keep the frontend lightweight, accessible, and bundler-free (see
`050-tooling.mdc`).

## Structure

- Semantic HTML5. One clear landmark structure (`header`, `main`, `footer`).
- Separate concerns: markup in HTML/Pug, styles in CSS/Sass, behaviour in JS.
- ES modules (`<script type="module">`); no global script soup.

## CSS

- Mobile-first, responsive layouts (Flexbox/Grid). Avoid fixed pixel widths
  for containers.
- Use CSS custom properties (design tokens) for color, spacing, and type.
- Prefer a small, hand-rolled stylesheet or a no-build framework. Do **not**
  pull in Tailwind/Bootstrap via a build step.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` and `prefers-color-scheme`.

## Accessibility

- All interactive elements keyboard-reachable with visible focus states.
- Label every form control; use ARIA only when native semantics fall short.
- Maintain WCAG AA color contrast.

## Performance

- No heavy frameworks for what plain DOM APIs can do.
- Lazy-load non-critical assets; keep total JS small.
- Optimize images before committing (size + format).
